From 0f2ddaf689d5a4ddfc0cd773da748912cc92a44e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:37:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(app): walk the selection once per input for the page

The Geometry tab asked operation::selection_account and the Contour
fields asked operation::contour_auto_side on each frame. Each ask ran
the full selection walk again: 4.2 ms and 4.1 ms per still frame in
release on fig8 with ten top chains (#2238 probe, state b).

The new operation/selection_memo.rs keeps one memo entry per input:
the setup, the picks and the parameters by value, and each world read
of the walk (facet allocation, pose, setup alignment, setup definition,
machine kind, WCS pose and word, document unit). One miss runs the walk
one time and keeps the notes, the door refusal and the Auto side.

Generation, the pick doors and the region walk do not read this memo.
They walk for themselves, so the side that the toolpath uses does not
change.

Pinned by contour_side_and_account_walk_once_per_input (every hit
equals a fresh walk, across picks, undo, a side edit and a part move)
and by the frame-cost probe (selections = 0 on still frames).

Fixes #2248
Fixes #2249

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
